# What must never reach a build context. The rule is not image size: anything
# copied in is in a layer, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
# image — so a .env in the context is a leaked credential even if no Dockerfile
# COPYs it by name.
#
# Check this file AND .gitignore whenever you add a file that could hold a
# secret. A leaked service-account key once matched neither of two patterns
# that were both supposed to catch it.

.env
.env.*
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

.git
.github
backups/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

node_modules/
dist/

# Per-context ignores: Docker reads the .dockerignore next to the CONTEXT root,
# not this one, for any build whose context is a subdirectory. backend/ and
# frontend/ therefore carry their own.
